      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:149:4",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ لَا بَأْسَ لِلْمُتَمَتِّعِ إِنْ لَمْ يُحْرِمْ مِنْ لَيْلَةِ التَّرْوِيَةِ مَتَى مَا تَيَسَّرَ لَهُ مَا لَمْ يَخَفْ فَوْتَ الْمَوْقِفَيْنِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ismail Bin Marrar, from Yunus, from Yaqoub Bin Shuayb Al Maysami who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘There is no problem for the performer of <span class=\"iTxt\">Tumatto</span> if he does not wear <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> from the night of Tarwiyya (8<sup>th</sup> Zil Hijjaj) whenever it is easy for him for as long as he does not fear losing the two pausing stations’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ‘Isma‘il ibn Marrar from Yunus from Ya’qub ibn Shu’ayb al-Mithamiy who has said the following: “I heard abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, say, ‘It is not harmful to one who is for al-Hajj al-Tamattu‘ (advantageous) to assume the state of Ihram in the night of al-Tarwiyah (eight of Dhu al-Hajj ah) whenever possible for him, as long as he is not afraid of losing the two al-Mawqafan (stations, Mina’ and ‘Arafat).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
